<p>SMS messages have an open rate of around 98%. That is not a typo. Nearly every text message you send gets read, and most of them get read within three minutes of landing. Compare that to email, which averages somewhere between 20% and 30%, and social media, where organic reach keeps shrinking year after year.</p>

<p>Despite those numbers, most small businesses either ignore SMS entirely or use it so poorly that it does more harm than good. They blast the same generic offer to their entire contact list, send messages at odd hours, forget to include an opt-out, or treat every text like a billboard ad. The result is unsubscribes, complaints, and a channel that never gets a fair chance.</p>

<p>The opportunity is massive. <a href="/blog/sms-marketing-small-business">SMS marketing</a> done well can drive bookings, recover lost revenue, boost reviews, and keep customers engaged between visits. This guide walks you through how to create campaigns that actually work, from compliance basics to message structure to measuring your return.</p>

