<h2>Campaign types that actually work</h2>

<p>Not all SMS campaigns are created equal. Some consistently outperform others because they match the strengths of the channel: short, timely, action-oriented, and personal. Here are the types that deliver real results for small businesses.</p>

<p><strong>Promotional offers and flash sales.</strong> Time-sensitive deals are perfect for SMS. "20% off all services this Friday only" creates urgency and drives quick action. The key is to make the offer genuinely valuable and truly time-limited. If every week brings another "exclusive" discount, people stop paying attention.</p>

<p><strong>Appointment reminders.</strong> This is arguably the highest-ROI use of SMS for service businesses. A simple reminder sequence, 24 hours before and again two hours before, can <a href="/blog/reduce-no-shows">cut your no-show rate significantly</a>. Include a confirmation link or a reply option so the customer can confirm or reschedule without calling.</p>

<p><strong>Review requests.</strong> Sending a text one to two days after a service with a direct link to your <a href="/blog/get-more-google-reviews">Google review page</a> is one of the easiest ways to build your online reputation. Keep it simple: "Hi [name], thanks for coming in. We would love a quick review if you have a moment: [link]."</p>

<p><strong>Post-service follow-ups.</strong> A brief check-in after a job is complete shows you care about the result, not just the sale. "Hi [name], just checking in to make sure everything is working well after your service on Tuesday. Let us know if you need anything." These messages build loyalty and often lead to repeat business.</p>

<p><strong>Re-engagement campaigns.</strong> Customers who have not visited or purchased in a while are not necessarily lost. A well-timed text can bring them back. "Hi [name], it has been a while since your last visit. We would love to see you again. Here is 15% off your next booking: [link]." Run these quarterly to keep your <a href="/blog/customer-follow-up-system">follow-up system</a> working even after the initial sequence ends.</p>

<p><strong>Loyalty and rewards notifications.</strong> If you run a loyalty program, SMS is the best channel for updates. "You are one visit away from a free [service]" is the kind of message people appreciate and act on. It reinforces the value of staying with your business.</p>

